            {
              "kind": "markdown",
              "text": "This project is a lightweight usage-analytics repo for GitHub Copilot Chat inside VS Code.\n\n- Core purpose: collect, normalize, and summarize Copilot usage from local VS Code data, then group it by workspace, model, and Jira-like ticket key.\n- Main implementation: `collectors/vscode/collect.py` reads VS Code’s local chat/session files (JSONL + SQLite), replays the mutation log to reconstruct each chat session, and computes usage totals like credits, tokens, and tool-call rounds.\n- Output: `reports/vscode-copilot.json` is a sample generated report showing totals, per-ticket usage, per-workspace usage, per-model usage, and per-session request details.\n- Structure:\n  - `collectors/vscode/README.md` documents the data model and how the collector works.\n  - `collectors/vscode/config.json` defines defaults for user directories, output format, and ticket prefix.\n  - `reports/` stores generated reports.\n- Important detail: it is a local reporting pipeline, not a web app or package project. It intentionally reads VS Code data on disk and avoids network calls.\n\nSo in short: this repo turns local Copilot Chat activity into a dashboard-style report for tracking usage and cost."
            }
